<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 303 0 R
/T (Measured signals using fNIRS are interpreted concerning physiological reactions associated with a neuronal activity change. In general, an increase of neuronal activity in the brain's specific area generates more blood flow, which in the fNIRS signal is visible as an increase in oxyhemoglobin and decreases the deoxyhemoglobin level.)
/E (Measured signals using fNIRS are interpreted concerning physiological reactions associated with a neuronal activity change. In general, an increase of neuronal activity in the brain's specific area generates more blood flow, which in the fNIRS signal is visible as an increase in oxyhemoglobin and decreases the deoxyhemoglobin level.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
