/Title (One consequence of failed calibration is channel overexposure, a situation in which the value for one or two infrared light wavelengths is outside the maximum detection range of signal receivers. This usually occurs when too much light passes through the tissue, such as in light-skinned subjects, children or short canals.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1709 0 R
/First 1720 0 R
/Last 1720 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
1716 0 obj
<<
