1729 0 obj
<<
/Title (From a technical point of view, the measurement of oxygenation changes in selected areas of the brain can be done using the so-called modified Beer-Lambert law. In a great simplification, if we know the tested substance's absorption characteristics and the intensity of the emitted and received light, we can estimate the changes of concentration analyzed substance. In our case, the emitted and received light is infrared waves, and the tested substances are oxy and deoxyhemoglobin. The modified Beer-Lambert law \(MBLL\) is the basis of continuous-wave near-infrared tissue spectroscopy \(cwNIRS\). The differential form of MBLL \(dMBLL\) states that the change in light attenuation is proportional to the changes in the concentrations of tissue chromophores, mainly oxy- and deoxyhaemoglobin.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1726 0 R
/First 1733 0 R
/Last 1733 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
